# Commit style

When the user asks to commit (including `/commit`), read and follow [`.cursor/skills/commit/SKILL.md`](../skills/commit/SKILL.md).

## Policy

- **Format:** `type(scope): description` — Conventional Commits, subject ≤ 50 chars, imperative, lowercase.
- **Release notes:** [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md) under **`## [Unreleased]`**, not commit subjects. Skill: **`peaky-changelog`**.
- **PRs:** squash title = commit subject for git history only.

Do not duplicate the full workflow here.
